    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test \u2014 the only test class in the project). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` alongside the fields it already emitted (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\nTo avoid duplicating the membership-number format, I extracted the formatting logic into a small single-responsibility helper and had both call sites use it:\n\n- **New `model/MembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 a static `of(Owner)` helper formatting `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, sitting alongside the existing `MembershipLevel` in the model package.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 its `membershipNumber(owner)` default now delegates to `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` instead of inlining the format (so the DTO and audit line can't drift apart).\n- **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 extended the `AUDIT.info` format/args with `membershipNumber={}` via `MembershipNumber.of(owner)`, and updated its Javadoc.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` asserts the audit line contains the fetched owner's `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`, and it passes.",
